@startuml Messy Wardrobe Tracker Class Diagram

title Personal Wardrobe Tracker - MESSY PROTOTYPE CLASS DIAGRAM\n(Intentionally Poor Design for Milestone 2)

' This diagram shows the intentionally poor design with violations of SOLID principles

package "wardrobe" {
    
    ' THE GOD CLASS - Does everything!
    class WardrobeApp {
        ' === DATA STORAGE (should be separate) ===
        - items: ArrayList<String[]>
        - outfits: ArrayList<String[]>
        - usageLogs: ArrayList<String[]>
        - DATA_FILE: String {static final}
        
        ' === UI COMPONENTS (should be separate) ===
        - tabbedPane: JTabbedPane
        - itemTable: JTable
        - itemTableModel: DefaultTableModel
        - outfitTable: JTable
        - outfitTableModel: DefaultTableModel
        - analyticsArea: JTextArea
        
        ' === CONSTRUCTOR ===
        + WardrobeApp()
        
        ' === UI INITIALIZATION (should be separate) ===
        - initUI(): void
        - createItemsPanel(): JPanel
        - createOutfitsPanel(): JPanel
        - createUsagePanel(): JPanel
        - createAnalyticsPanel(): JPanel
        - createSearchPanel(): JPanel
        
        ' === ITEM MANAGEMENT (should be in separate class) ===
        - addItemDialog(): void
        - editItemDialog(): void
        - deleteItem(): void
        - refreshItemTable(): void
        
        ' === OUTFIT MANAGEMENT (should be in separate class) ===
        - createOutfitDialog(): void
        - deleteOutfit(): void
        - refreshOutfitTable(): void
        
        ' === USAGE TRACKING (should be in separate class) ===
        - logItemUsage(JTextArea): void
        - logOutfitUsage(JTextArea): void
        - displayUsageHistory(JTextArea): void
        
        ' === ANALYTICS (should be in separate class) ===
        - calculateAndDisplayAnalytics(): void
        
        ' === FILE I/O (should be in separate repository class) ===
        - saveDataToFile(): void
        - loadDataFromFile(): void
        
        ' === MAIN ===
        + {static} main(String[]): void
    }
    
    note right of WardrobeApp
        **MASSIVE GOD CLASS**
        
        Violations:
        • Single Responsibility Principle
          - Handles UI rendering
          - Handles business logic
          - Handles data persistence
          - Handles analytics calculations
        
        • Open/Closed Principle
          - Hardcoded filter logic
          - Hardcoded categories
          - Can't extend without modification
        
        • Liskov Substitution
          - No inheritance hierarchy
        
        • Interface Segregation
          - No interfaces defined
        
        • Dependency Inversion
          - Depends on concrete Swing classes
          - Depends on concrete file system
          - No abstractions anywhere
        
        Other Issues:
        • Tight coupling everywhere
        • Code duplication (add/edit dialogs)
        • Poor data structures (String arrays!)
        • No validation abstraction
        • No proper domain models
        • Business logic in UI handlers
        • 1000+ lines in single class
    end note
    
    ' External dependencies (concrete implementations only!)
    WardrobeApp ..> JFrame : extends
    WardrobeApp ..> ArrayList : uses
    WardrobeApp ..> JTabbedPane : uses
    WardrobeApp ..> JTable : uses
    WardrobeApp ..> DefaultTableModel : uses
    WardrobeApp ..> JTextArea : uses
    WardrobeApp ..> JPanel : creates
    WardrobeApp ..> JDialog : creates
    WardrobeApp ..> JButton : creates
    WardrobeApp ..> JTextField : creates
    WardrobeApp ..> JComboBox : creates
    WardrobeApp ..> FileWriter : uses directly
    WardrobeApp ..> FileReader : uses directly
    WardrobeApp ..> BufferedWriter : uses directly
    WardrobeApp ..> BufferedReader : uses directly
}

note as N1
    **What's Wrong With This Design?**
    
    1. **God Class Anti-Pattern**
       - WardrobeApp does literally everything
       - Over 1000 lines of code in one class
       - Impossible to test individual components
    
    2. **No Abstraction**
       - Data stored as String arrays (not objects)
       - No Item, Outfit, or UsageLog classes
       - No interfaces for extensibility
    
    3. **Tight Coupling**
       - UI directly manipulates data structures
       - Business logic embedded in event handlers
       - File I/O mixed with business logic
    
    4. **No Separation of Concerns**
       - Presentation, business, and data layers all mixed
       - Can't change UI without risking business logic
       - Can't change storage without touching UI
    
    5. **Hardcoded Logic**
       - Filter types hardcoded with if-else chains
       - Categories hardcoded in dropdown arrays
       - Can't add new filters without modifying code
    
    6. **Code Duplication**
       - Add and Edit dialogs share 90% code
       - Validation logic repeated everywhere
       - Table refresh logic duplicated
    
    7. **Poor Error Handling**
       - Catches exceptions but just prints stack traces
       - No recovery mechanisms
       - No validation abstraction
    
    8. **Fragile Data Persistence**
       - Custom text format with | delimiter
       - No version control
       - String parsing can easily break
       - No transaction support
end note

@enduml

